<title>UK: EU grants free-mkt barley, soft wheat.</title>
<headline>EU grants free-mkt barley, soft wheat.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union on Thursday granted the following licences to export free market grain to non-EU countries, member-country officials said.</p>
<p>		  Tonnage	  Maximum rebate</p>
<p>Soft wheat    115,500	  17.99  ecu/tonne</p>
<p>Barley	  180,000	  27.94  ecu/tonne</p>
<p>Durum wheat     5,500	   5.95  ecu/tonne</p>
<p>Rye		 1,000	  30.98  ecu/tonne</p>
<p>Greek Maize    10,000	  38.43  ecu/tonne</p>
<p>Bids for oats from Sweden and Finland were rejected, as were bids for Swedish intervention barley.</p>
<p>--Christopher Lyddon, London newsroom +44 171 542 7928</p>
</text>
